# 100% Free Stack: Cloudflare D1 + ImageKit (20 GB Free Storage)
### Strictly NO Credit Card / Payment Method Required!

This setup provides:
1. **ImageKit.io**: **20 GB free file storage** + 20 GB/month bandwidth for your PDFs & documents.
2. **Cloudflare D1**: Serverless SQL database (free, no credit card required).
3. **Cloudflare Worker**: Secure backend API connecting your website to D1 and ImageKit.

---

## Step 1: Get Free 20 GB Storage on ImageKit (No Credit Card)

1. Go to [imagekit.io/registration](https://imagekit.io/registration) and sign up with your Google account or email. *(No credit card is asked).*
2. Choose any name for your ImageKit ID (e.g., `campusvault`).
3. Once inside the ImageKit dashboard:
   - In the left sidebar, click **Developer options** (or the gear icon).
   - Look under **API keys**:
   - Copy your **Private API key** (it looks like `private_...`).

---

## Step 2: Set Up Cloudflare D1 Database (No Credit Card)

1. Go to [dash.cloudflare.com](https://dash.cloudflare.com/) and log in.
2. In the left menu, click **Storage & Databases** > **D1 SQL Database**.
3. Click **Create database** > Name it `campusvault-db` > Click **Create**.
4. Click on `campusvault-db` and select the **Console** tab.
5. Paste the contents of [`schema.sql`](file:///c:/Study%20BTECH/CampusVoice/CollegeHelper/schema.sql):
   ```sql
   CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS materials (
       id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
       title TEXT NOT NULL,
       type TEXT NOT NULL,
       author TEXT NOT NULL,
       college TEXT NOT NULL,
       subject TEXT NOT NULL,
       description TEXT,
       date TEXT NOT NULL,
       fileName TEXT NOT NULL,
       rating_sum INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
       rating_count INTEGER DEFAULT 0
   );

   CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_materials_college ON materials(college);
   CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_materials_subject ON materials(subject);
   CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_materials_type ON materials(type);
   ```
6. Click **Execute**. Your database table is created!

---

## Step 3: Deploy the Cloudflare Worker API

1. In Cloudflare, go to **Compute (Workers & Pages)** > **Workers & Pages**.
2. Click **Create application** > **Create Worker** > Name it `campusvault-api` > Click **Deploy**.
3. Click **Edit code**:
   - Copy the entire code from [`worker.js`](file:///c:/Study%20BTECH/CampusVoice/CollegeHelper/worker.js) and paste it into Cloudflare's code editor.
   - Click **Deploy**.
4. Configure the D1 Database binding:
   - Go back to Worker page > **Settings** > **Bindings**.
   - Under **D1 Database Bindings**, click **Add**:
     - Variable name: `DB`
     - D1 database: `campusvault-db`
   - Click **Save and Deploy**.
5. Add your ImageKit Private Key:
   - In Worker **Settings** > **Variables and Secrets** (or **Environment Variables**):
     - Click **Add**:
     - Variable name: `IMAGEKIT_PRIVATE_KEY`
     - Value: Paste your `private_...` key from ImageKit.
     - Click **Save and Deploy**.
6. Copy your Worker URL (e.g., `https://campusvault-api.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev`).

---

## Step 4: Connect Frontend (`static/app.js`)

Open [`static/app.js`](file:///c:/Study%20BTECH/CampusVoice/CollegeHelper/static/app.js#L57):
Find line 57:
```javascript
const API_BASE_URL = 'https://campusvault-api.YOUR_SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev';
```
Replace it with your real Worker URL (e.g. `https://campusvault-api.yourname.workers.dev`).

---

## How It Works

1. When a student fills out the **Contribute** form and selects a PDF, the file is sent to your **Cloudflare Worker**.
2. The Worker securely uploads the PDF to **ImageKit** using your private key (20 GB free storage, fast global CDN).
3. ImageKit returns the permanent download link (e.g., `https://ik.imagekit.io/.../notes.pdf`).
4. The Worker saves the material details and download link into **Cloudflare D1**.
5. When students browse CampusVault, all materials are loaded instantly, and clicking **Download** streams the file directly from ImageKit!
